# Everything ignored here is either an INPUT dropped in by hand or an OUTPUT
# the tools regenerate. AGENTS.md explains each one under "Repository layout".

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Input: the upstream release archive. Hundreds of megabytes, versioned by
# whoever cut it, and not ours to redistribute. Drop the current one in the
# repository root; build-dist.py finds it by extension.
#
# Anchored to the root on purpose: an unanchored *.zip would also swallow a
# test fixture or sample archive committed deeper in the tree.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
/*.7z
/*.rar
/*.zip
/*.tar.gz
/*.tgz

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Outputs, all reproducible from the archive by `python crossbuild/build-dist.py`
#   extracted/  the unpacked archive, ~1.3 GB, dominated by Data/cbdb.db
#   dist/       one assembled folder per target, each with its own copy of the
#               1.3 GB database
#   packages/   the shippable archives, ~390 MB each
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
/extracted/
/dist/
/packages/
# The build assembles beside the real directory and swaps in on success.
# An interrupted run leaves these behind, full of upstream payload.
/extracted.incoming/
/extracted.old/


# Parked upstream tooling that build-dist.py does not ship and does not build:
# the database-build binaries and the schema/codegen scripts. All of it comes
# out of the upstream archive, so committing it would duplicate the input.
/maintainer-tools/

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Local settings
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Machine-specific paths, and a pointer to an archive that is not ours to
# redistribute. .env.sample is the committed template.
# .env* rather than .env: a .env.ci or .env.bak holds the same machine
# paths and would otherwise be committable.
.env*
!.env.sample

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Data, belt and braces
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# The directories above already cover every one of these in practice. They are
# repeated as bare patterns so that a database, a WAL sidecar or a release
# archive left ANYWHERE in the tree -- a stray copy, a hand-made test folder,
# an experiment under crossbuild/ -- cannot be committed by accident. A single
# cbdb.db is 1.3 GB and GitHub refuses pushes over 100 MB per file, so one
# mistake here costs a rewritten history rather than a revert.
*.db
*.db-wal
*.db-shm
*.sqlite
*.sqlite3
cbdb.db*
# Uncompressed tarballs are not covered by the .tar.gz pattern above.
*.tar

# Compiled output. A stray cbdb.exe copied beside the tracked files is tens
# of megabytes; the shim and the Go objects are the same class of litter.
# Nothing in this repository is a committed binary except the icon and the
# logo. The extensionless names are the macOS binaries, which carry no
# suffix -- a glob cannot catch those, so they are listed.
*.exe
*.o
*.a
/cbdb
/crossbuild/ccwrap/ccwrap

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Scratch
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# build-dist.py puts its staging tree, cc shims and zig cache outside the
# repository, at C:\cbdb-dist-build -- Go splits $CC on whitespace, so the shim
# must not live under a path containing any. This pattern only matters if
# someone points --work at the repository.
/cbdb-dist-build/
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]

# Built by `go build` in ccwrap/ by hand. The real build compiles the shim into
# the scratch directory instead, so a binary here is always a stray.
/crossbuild/ccwrap/ccwrap.exe

# Generated from the logo by make-favicon.py. favicon.ico IS committed, because
# build-dist.py needs it and regenerating it would otherwise make Pillow and
# numpy a hard requirement for a plain build. These two are only ever looked at
# by a human tuning the artwork.
/crossbuild/assets/favicon-preview.png
/crossbuild/assets/logo-crimson.png

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# OS and editor noise
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
Thumbs.db
desktop.ini
.DS_Store
._*
.vscode/
.idea/
*.swp
